<https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Software/packageUrl> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "A package URL (commonly pronounced and referred to as \"purl\") is an attempt to standardize package representations\nin order to reliably identify and locate software packages.\nA packageUrl is a URL string which represents a package in a\nmostly universal and uniform way across programming languages, package\nmanagers, packaging conventions, tools, APIs and databases.\n\nA packageUrl is composed of seven components:\n\nscheme:type/namespace/name@version?qualifiers#subpath\n\n\nThe definition for each component can be found in the corresponding\nAnnex of this document.\nKnown type definitions can be found in the\nPackage URL type definitions <https://github.com/package-url/purl-spec/blob/b33dda1cf4515efa8eabbbe8e9b140950805f845/PURL-TYPES.rst>.\n\nComponents are designed such that they form a hierarchy from the most\nsignificant on the left to the least significant components on the right."@en .
_:N6da1a5e54c8a424f9bc8419af63a13f0 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/SupplyChain/ChangeProcess> .
<https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/inspection> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A thorough examination or checking of documentation, records, processes, or systems to confirm compliance or adherence. An inspection needs to have a defined set of acceptance criteria (e.g. a checklist), a documentation of roles involved in the inspection (e.g. to document the inspector's independence) and a clear documentation of when and how it was performed."@en .
<https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/ProfileIdentifierType/simpleLicensing> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The element follows the SimpleLicensing profile specification."@en .
<https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/other> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Used when the type does not match any of the other options."@en .
<https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Software/Sbom> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Sbom"@en .
